    {
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 15 - EGX Backtest\n\nReplays the scanner pipeline (04-11) once per historical trading date between startDate and endDate, tagging every simulated run as scanner_runs.run_type = 'BACKTEST' so it never collides with real daily runs. Each date is processed sequentially and only ever touches data with trading_date <= that date — the same point-in-time workflows used for live scanning, so there is no separate 'backtest scoring logic' to drift out of sync with production (spec section 30).\n\nParameters (pass via Execute Workflow, or edit 'Resolve Backtest Parameters' defaults for a Manual Trigger run):\n`startDate`, `endDate`, `minimumScore` (default 0), `setupType` (default 'ANY'), `topN` (default 10).\n\n**Expensive**: runs the full pipeline once PER trading day in range. A 90-day backtest over ~250 stocks is a lot of Postgres round-trips — expect this to take a while. Start with a short date range.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "35596aad-9319-4962-b62b-188567fecdca"
    },
    {
      "name": "Manual Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "parameters": {},
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "id": "821a20b1-4d4e-43af-b975-1cda52e83be0"
    },
    {
      "name": "When Executed by Another Workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "passthrough"
      },
      "position": [
        260,
        0
      ],
      "id": "3d50ea52-a8f1-45a7-b41c-a1431532beab"
    },
    {
      "name": "Resolve Backtest Parameters",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// the trigger lookup THROWS if that trigger never executed (e.g. this workflow\n// run via Manual Trigger alone) — confirmed via live E2E testing. try/catch\n// makes \"never executed\" and \"executed with zero items\" behave the same.\nlet trigger = {};\ntry {\n  const triggerItems = $('When Executed by Another Workflow').all();\n  trigger = triggerItems.length ? triggerItems[0].json : {};\n} catch (e) { trigger = {}; }\n\nconst today = new Date();\nconst defaultEnd = new Date(today);\ndefaultEnd.setDate(defaultEnd.getDate() - 1);\nconst defaultStart = new Date(defaultEnd);\ndefaultStart.setDate(defaultStart.getDate() - 90);\n\nconst startDate = trigger.startDate || defaultStart.toISOString().slice(0, 10);\nconst endDate = trigger.endDate || defaultEnd.toISOString().slice(0, 10);\nconst minimumScore = isFinite(Number(trigger.minimumScore)) ? Number(trigger.minimumScore) : 0;\nconst setupType = trigger.setupType || 'ANY';\nconst topN = Number(trigger.topN) || Number($env.TOP_N) || 10;\n\nreturn [{ json: { startDate, endDate, minimumScore, setupType, topN } }];"
      },
      "position": [
        520,
        0
      ],
      "id": "00aae1c3-3f2b-4594-892f-b225e8ecee70"
    },
    {
      "name": "Get Trading Dates In Range",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "SELECT DISTINCT trading_date::text AS trading_date FROM daily_prices\nWHERE trading_date BETWEEN $1 AND $2\nORDER BY trading_date ASC;",
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ [$json.startDate, $json.endDate] }}"
        }
      },
      "executeOnce": true,
      "position": [
        780,
        0
      ],
      "id": "827a091c-2c65-46b1-9f24-8c847830b753"
    },
